   PNG checks per engine. No page errors or console warnings/errors occur.
+
+### F-309 - A missing accessible name failed inside markup escaping
+
+- Status: resolved
+- Severity: low
+- Owner: API
+- Observed in: Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/chartRender.tsx`)
+- Friction: chart titles there are user-authored and may be empty, so every
+  `<Chart>` guards `ariaLabel={title || fallback}`. Checking what an unguarded
+  value does showed that `renderChartSvg(scene, {})`, the Canvas shell
+  prerender, and adapter prerender threw this error from attribute escaping:
+  `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'replace')`. Mounting set the
+  attribute to `"undefined"`, and an empty string produced an unnamed
+  `role="img"` surface. The type requires the option, so only untyped or
+  loosely typed callers hit it, but nothing in the failure named `ariaLabel`.
+- Decision: validate `ariaLabel` where markup is written and where a host
+  mounts or updates, throwing a `TypeError` with the message
+  `A chart requires a non-empty ariaLabel string`. Keep the option type
+  unchanged.
+- Verification: SVG, Canvas, composed-layer, `mountCanvasChart`, and adapter
+  prerender, mount, and update regressions fail before and pass after. An
+  invalid update leaves the previous label mounted.
